  "readme": {
    "available": true,
    "excerpt": "Host-side crash/restart watchdog for dsh. When the dsh server process dies — a crash, OOM, kill -9, or a restart — every running agent is interrupted and the work simply stops. The persisted session logs survive, but nothing picks the work back up until a human reopens the sessio"
